# client-custom-fields.absent-scope-matrix.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: AC-37 (the scope matrix is readable as a VALUE at run time —
# `useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix` deep-equals
# `CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELDS_SCOPE_MATRIX`) —
# client-custom-fields.surface.test.ts:185-189, the
# "AC-37 useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix is wired and deep-equals the
# declared collection matrix" case.
#
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# REBASED (2026-08-22, developer seat, factory run) — the prior hunk dropped
# the third `createScopedComposable` argument at the lazy-registration call
# (`useClientCustomFields.ts:163-171`). That argument's own
# `composable.scopeMatrix = scopeMatrix` assignment (`scope.builder.ts:455`)
# lands on the INNER deferred registration function
# (`registeredUseClientCustomFields`), never on the EXPORTED
# `useClientCustomFields` symbol AC-37 actually reads (no call —
# `useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix` off the function itself). This
# module's own `@decision` block (`useClientCustomFields.ts:175-195`)
# documents why a SEPARATE explicit assignment exists for exactly that
# reason. Traced against AC-37's now-live spec, the old hunk is INERT:
# dropping the call's third argument leaves that separate assignment
# untouched, so `useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix` still deep-equals the
# real matrix and the AC-37 assertion stays GREEN — a dead control. This
# rebase moves the mutation onto the line that actually wires the EXPORTED
# symbol, preserving the same capability under test ("the module publishes
# its own scope matrix as a value") — the exact advertised-but-absent
# capability AC-37 exists to catch, and the same downstream defect
# `scope-utils.ts:42` (playground `servesActor`, out of this suite's reach
# per the AC-37 docblock) is guarded against: an absent matrix makes
# `servesActor` return `true` for every actor instead of refusing one.
#
# Mutates: useClientCustomFields.ts — deletes the explicit
# `(useClientCustomFields as ScopedComposable<...>).scopeMatrix =
# CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELDS_SCOPE_MATRIX;` statement. The `@decision` doc block
# immediately above it is left standing — the code no longer does what its
# own doc block says it does, which is the point of the mutation.
#
# Expected RED: `useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix` reads `undefined`
# instead of deep-equal to `CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELDS_SCOPE_MATRIX` —
# client-custom-fields.surface.test.ts's AC-37
# "useClientCustomFields.scopeMatrix is wired and deep-equals the declared
# collection matrix" assertion goes RED.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>     # mutate
#   pnpm test client-custom-fields.surface.test.ts    # must go RED
#   git apply -R <this file>  # revert — must return to green
#
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFields.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFields.ts
@@ -193,12 +193,6 @@
  *   copied off `registeredUseClientCustomFields` — still `undefined` until
  *   the first call, and `useModulePort` reads it before any call happens.
  */
-(
-  useClientCustomFields as ScopedComposable<
-    ReturnType<typeof createClientCustomFieldsForScope>,
-    ClientCustomFieldsScopeMatrix
-  >
-).scopeMatrix = CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELDS_SCOPE_MATRIX;
 
 // Type export for consumers
 export type UseClientCustomFields = ReturnType<typeof useClientCustomFields>;
